<!--
  Slim-list row surface: a full pill.

  The corner radius is exactly half the row height declared in oneui_recents_card_slim.xml (64dp),
  which is what makes the ends semicircular rather than merely rounded. The two numbers have to move
  together — a radius smaller than half the height turns the pill back into a rounded rectangle, and
  a larger one is silently clamped by the renderer, so the shape would stop tracking the layout.

  Near-black, but not opaque: recents draws over the live wallpaper (the host lays down a light
  #33000000 veil, not a scrim), and letting a tenth of that through is what keeps the rows sitting
  *on* the wallpaper instead of punching holes in it. On the 1080p/420dpi reference frame that lands
  the fill between #000000 and #191919, which is where the One UI original measures.
-->
<shape xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:shape="rectangle">
    <solid android:color="#E6000000" />
    <corners android:radius="32dp" />
</shape>
